  "verbalization": "Gilteritinib is associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia With Minimal Differentiation through a pathway involving Glasdegib, which appears in multiple indirect relationships. The evidence suggests that Gilteritinib may be repurposed for this leukemia subtype, as it shares a common indication with Glasdegib, which in turn is linked to the target condition. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with some variation in the strength of the connections. The presence of Glasdegib in multiple pathways suggests a potential mechanism where Gilteritinib could interact with Glasdegib to exert therapeutic effects on this leukemia subtype. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Gilteritinib in the treatment of Acute Myeloid Leukemia With Minimal Differentiation, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and clinical relevance."
